RoboCodify uses PyRUA-Lean's existing Python cells, public robot APIs,
perception/motion tools, and recovery guidance. The experimental prompt appendix
builds on that guidance. The external launcher follows our earlier integration
with PyRUA-Lean's build_prompt/play.main entrypoints. It adds a workspace module
and an initial prompt appendix, without replacing the controller or evaluator.
The core recovery module and prompt are our experimental additions; this repository
does not claim authorship of the upstream cells, geometry methods or robot primitives.

The test suite imports the separately obtained, fixed PyRUA-Lean checkout.
Its complete original NOTICE is retained in third_party/PyRUA-Lean-NOTICE for
attribution context; the referenced RPent and GenieSim implementations/assets
are not redistributed by RoboCodify.

PyRUA-Lean paper:
  Fewer Tokens, Better Action: GPT-6 Astra Robot Agents with 14% Higher
  Success Rate but 65% Fewer Tokens. arXiv:2610.01939.
  https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.01939

tests/fixtures/recovery_before_compaction.py is our frozen earlier recovery
implementation, retained only for a behavioral regression comparison.
See provenance.json for original file hashes and migration changes.

RoboDojo task definitions, layouts, assets, native scoring and simulator code
are external dependencies. Existing experiments include documented compatibility
adaptations and are not presented as official current-protocol benchmark results.
